{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation notes (2026-11-18 PST)\n- Committed 92f76b42f92 locally (worktree c2-gate-owner-lock), waiting for a `make verify` slot.\n- Change from the plan: no `# mechanism-ok` marker. The mechanism census records presence per name, and `lock::.lock` is already in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (another `.lock` literal), so the new literal adds no new or increased mechanism. `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 without a marker.\n- Poller side: `_owner_lock_held` opens the lock file without creating it. A missing file, a lock it can take, or a probe error means no live owner, so jobs from before this change, and platforms without a lock primitive, keep the registry rule. Two pollers probing at the same instant can see each other's probe as a live owner; that only delays a stale verdict by one poll.\n- Tests: `test_gate_status_keeps_a_job_whose_owner_in_another_process_is_alive` (a helper process started with `sys.executable` holds the lock; `gate_status` stays `running` and the index bytes are unchanged; after the helper exits, it materializes `failed / daemon-stopped`), and `test_review_plan_start_holds_the_owner_lock_until_the_terminal_record`. All 41 tests in `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py` pass.\n- Portability: `lock_kernel` provides both legs (flock / msvcrt.locking). The deletion after release is best-effort, so a Windows handle still open in a prober leaves the file behind, which reads as \"no owner\". No fork, signals, pass_fds or fixed /tmp paths. The Windows sweep will be dispatched after merge."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795069853374796948,"uuid":"d987cff0-f9cf-4040-863c-829f827d7080"}